Perfect. Now I have enough context. Let me create a comprehensive design document.

Based on my analysis of the UDAF model implementation in `/Users/ab/Projects/spec-oracle/spec-core/src/udaf.rs` and its usage throughout the codebase, I can now provide a comprehensive type-safety design.

## Design Analysis

### Current Problems Identified

1. **String IDs everywhere**: Universe.id, Domain.id, AdmissibleSet.spec_id, TransformFunction.id
2. **No compile-time validation**: IDs like "U0", "U1" are created via `format!("U{}", layer)` but nothing prevents typos
3. **HashMap<String, String> metadata**: Keys like "universe", "source_file", "rpc_name", "extractor", "inferred" are all stringly-typed
4. **Reference integrity**: HashSet<String> for specifications, covered_by, contradicts - no guarantee referenced IDs exist
5. **ID generation inconsistency**: Some use UUID, some use formatted strings, some are ad-hoc

### Metadata Keys Found in Codebase
- "universe" - Universe identifier for inter-universe analysis
- "source_file" - File path where spec was extracted
- "rpc_name" - gRPC RPC method name
- "extractor" - Which extractor generated the spec (function_name, assertion, test, doc, proto_rpc, etc.)
- "inferred" - Boolean marker for inferred specs
- "variable" - Variable name in constraints
- "impl_code", "test_code" - Code snippets
- "pattern", "value", "min", "max", "source" - Constraint extraction metadata

## Type-Safe Design

### 1. ID Type System

```rust
// spec-core/src/udaf/ids.rs

use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};
use std::fmt;
use std::str::FromStr;

/// Universe ID with compile-time layer validation
#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq, Hash, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub struct UniverseId(String);

impl UniverseId {
    /// Create root universe U0
    pub const fn root() -> Self {
        UniverseId(String::from("U0"))
    }

    /// Create projection universe from layer (U1, U2, U3, ...)
    pub fn projection(layer: u8) -> Result<Self, IdError> {
        if layer == 0 {
            return Err(IdError::InvalidLayer("U0 is reserved for root universe".into()));
        }
        Ok(UniverseId(format!("U{}", layer)))
    }

    /// Parse from string (for deserialization/user input)
    pub fn parse(s: &str) -> Result<Self, IdError> {
        if !s.starts_with('U') {
            return Err(IdError::InvalidFormat("Universe ID must start with 'U'".into()));
        }
        let layer_str = &s[1..];
        if layer_str.is_empty() {
            return Err(IdError::InvalidFormat("Missing layer number".into()));
        }
        // Validate it's a number
        layer_str.parse::<u8>()
            .map_err(|_| IdError::InvalidFormat("Layer must be a number".into()))?;
        Ok(UniverseId(s.to_string()))
    }

    pub fn as_str(&self) -> &str {
        &self.0
    }

    pub fn layer(&self) -> u8 {
        self.0[1..].parse().unwrap_or(0)
    }
}

impl fmt::Display for UniverseId {
    fn fmt(&self, f: &mut fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> fmt::Result {
        write!(f, "{}", self.0)
    }
}

impl FromStr for UniverseId {
    type Err = IdError;
    fn from_str(s: &str) -> Result<Self, Self::Err> {
        UniverseId::parse(s)
    }
}

/// Domain identifier (UUID-based for uniqueness)
#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq, Hash, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub struct DomainId(String);

impl DomainId {
    pub fn new() -> Self {
        DomainId(uuid::Uuid::new_v4().to_string())
    }

    pub fn from_uuid(id: uuid::Uuid) -> Self {
        DomainId(id.to_string())
    }

    pub fn parse(s: &str) -> Result<Self, IdError> {
        // Validate UUID format
        uuid::Uuid::parse_str(s)
            .map_err(|_| IdError::InvalidFormat("Domain ID must be valid UUID".into()))?;
        Ok(DomainId(s.to_string()))
    }

    pub fn as_str(&self) -> &str {
        &self.0
    }
}

/// Specification node identifier (UUID-based)
#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq, Hash, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub struct SpecId(String);

impl SpecId {
    pub fn new() -> Self {
        SpecId(uuid::Uuid::new_v4().to_string())
    }

    pub fn from_uuid(id: uuid::Uuid) -> Self {
        SpecId(id.to_string())
    }

    pub fn parse(s: &str) -> Result<Self, IdError> {
        uuid::Uuid::parse_str(s)
            .map_err(|_| IdError::InvalidFormat("Spec ID must be valid UUID".into()))?;
        Ok(SpecId(s.to_string()))
    }

    pub fn as_str(&self) -> &str {
        &self.0
    }
}

/// Transform function identifier (formatted: f_SOURCE_to_TARGET)
#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq, Hash, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub struct TransformId(String);

impl TransformId {
    /// Create inverse transform ID: f_Ui_to_U0
    pub fn inverse(source: &UniverseId) -> Self {
        TransformId(format!("f_{}_to_U0", source.as_str()))
    }

    /// Create forward transform ID: f_SOURCE_TARGET
    pub fn forward(source: &UniverseId, target: &UniverseId) -> Self {
        TransformId(format!("f_{}_{}", source.as_str(), target.as_str()))
    }

    pub fn parse(s: &str) -> Result<Self, IdError> {
        if !s.starts_with("f_") {
            return Err(IdError::InvalidFormat("Transform ID must start with 'f_'".into()));
        }
        Ok(TransformId(s.to_string()))
    }

    pub fn as_str(&self) -> &str {
        &self.0
    }
}

#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]
pub enum IdError {
    #[error("Invalid ID format: {0}")]
    InvalidFormat(String),
    #[error("Invalid layer: {0}")]
    InvalidLayer(String),
}
```

### 2. Strongly-Typed Metadata

```rust
// spec-core/src/udaf/metadata.rs

use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};
use std::collections::HashMap;

/// Metadata key types (compile-time validation)
#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq, Hash, Serialize, Deserialize)]
#[serde(rename_all = "snake_case")]
pub enum MetadataKey {
    Universe,
    SourceFile,
    RpcName,
    Extractor,
    Inferred,
    Variable,
    ImplCode,
    TestCode,
    Pattern,
    Value,
    Min,
    Max,
    Source,
    /// Extension point for custom keys
    Custom(String),
}

impl MetadataKey {
    pub fn as_str(&self) -> &str {
        match self {
            MetadataKey::Universe => "universe",
            MetadataKey::SourceFile => "source_file",
            MetadataKey::RpcName => "rpc_name",
            MetadataKey::Extractor => "extractor",
            MetadataKey::Inferred => "inferred",
            MetadataKey::Variable => "variable",
            MetadataKey::ImplCode => "impl_code",
            MetadataKey::TestCode => "test_code",
            MetadataKey::Pattern => "pattern",
            MetadataKey::Value => "value",
            MetadataKey::Min => "min",
            MetadataKey::Max => "max",
            MetadataKey::Source => "source",
            MetadataKey::Custom(s) => s,
        }
    }
}

impl From<&str> for MetadataKey {
    fn from(s: &str) -> Self {
        match s {
            "universe" => MetadataKey::Universe,
            "source_file" => MetadataKey::SourceFile,
            "rpc_name" => MetadataKey::RpcName,
            "extractor" => MetadataKey::Extractor,
            "inferred" => MetadataKey::Inferred,
            "variable" => MetadataKey::Variable,
            "impl_code" => MetadataKey::ImplCode,
            "test_code" => MetadataKey::TestCode,
            "pattern" => MetadataKey::Pattern,
            "value" => MetadataKey::Value,
            "min" => MetadataKey::Min,
            "max" => MetadataKey::Max,
            "source" => MetadataKey::Source,
            _ => MetadataKey::Custom(s.to_string()),
        }
    }
}

/// Type-safe metadata container
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Default, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub struct Metadata {
    entries: HashMap<String, String>,
}

impl Metadata {
    pub fn new() -> Self {
        Self { entries: HashMap::new() }
    }

    pub fn insert(&mut self, key: MetadataKey, value: impl Into<String>) {
        self.entries.insert(key.as_str().to_string(), value.into());
    }

    pub fn get(&self, key: &MetadataKey) -> Option<&String> {
        self.entries.get(key.as_str())
    }

    pub fn get_str(&self, key: &MetadataKey) -> Option<&str> {
        self.entries.get(key.as_str()).map(|s| s.as_str())
    }

    pub fn contains_key(&self, key: &MetadataKey) -> bool {
        self.entries.contains_key(key.as_str())
    }

    pub fn remove(&mut self, key: &MetadataKey) -> Option<String> {
        self.entries.remove(key.as_str())
    }

    /// Access raw HashMap for backward compatibility
    pub fn raw(&self) -> &HashMap<String, String> {
        &self.entries
    }

    /// Mutable access to raw HashMap (use sparingly)
    pub fn raw_mut(&mut self) -> &mut HashMap<String, String> {
        &mut self.entries
    }
}

// Specialized metadata types for each UDAF component

/// Universe metadata
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub struct UniverseMetadata {
    base: Metadata,
}

impl UniverseMetadata {
    pub fn new() -> Self {
        Self { base: Metadata::new() }
    }

    pub fn metadata(&self) -> &Metadata {
